WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:04.290
Today, we're going to talk about three
things that I wish I had when I went to

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:09.080
law school- things which I still use
today as a practicing attorney, so stick around.

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:16.180
Before we begin, a little background.

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:17.800
This is a casebook.

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:22.040
You'll get a case book for every single one of
your law school classes, and a case book

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:27.599
is exactly what it sounds like it's a
book full of cases. Now, I hate case books.

00:00:27.599 --> 00:00:33.420
Why? They're big, they're heavy, they're
expensive, and what you'll find is that

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:38.340
the authors of case books are incredibly
lazy. Why? Well theoretically, they're

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:42.210
supposed to go through the cases that
they include in their case books and

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:47.340
only include the most important material.
In practice, that's not what they do.

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:53.190
In fact, in practice authors simply include the cases verbatim, which means you're

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:57.809
paying hundreds of dollars for cases
that are in the public domain and you

00:00:57.809 --> 00:01:02.609
can access for free. These things are
heavy. As a result some people will take

00:01:02.609 --> 00:01:07.710
those wheelie bags that you'll see in
airports. When I went to law school, I

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:12.270
often tore the pages out of the case
books, because I hated transporting these

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:16.979
damn things to class. And that brings me
to the first thing that I wish I had in

00:01:16.979 --> 00:01:25.080
law school, and that's this: a beautiful
shiny tablet. Technology has progressed

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:28.710
so far that so many of the tablets out
there are great - it doesn't need to be an

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:34.700
iPad, but the reason a tablet is great is
because you can access all of your cases

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:39.810
through the iPad and specifically what I
use is called WestlawNext. It's an app

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:44.579
for the iPad. Now in law school, you're
going to get free access to West Law.

00:01:44.579 --> 00:01:50.360
It's one of the two major case databases,
and what's great is you can go online

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:56.719
access your cases and read them there. So
instead of transporting your big heavy

00:01:56.719 --> 00:02:01.860
useless case books you can just bring
one tablet or your laptop if you want to

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:06.600
to class. When you use a tablet to read
your cases they will give you the

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:10.530
bright-line rule that's the thing that
is most important about your case right

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:15.420
up front in the head notes. 
And as a bonus, you can use a good tablet

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:20.189
as a second monitor for your laptop.
There are inexpensive apps that let you

00:02:20.189 --> 00:02:26.310
use your iPad as an extension of your
laptop. I wish I had a really good tablet

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:30.420
when I went to law school. It would have
saved so much time - it would have saved

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:35.760
my back so much trouble from having to
carry these case books around all the time.

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:37.400
So that brings me to the second thing

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:41.519
that I wish I had when I started law
school and that's this: a really nice

00:02:41.519 --> 00:02:46.859
laptop- with a solid state hard drive a
long battery life and cloud storage. Now

00:02:46.859 --> 00:02:51.689
every single lawyer that I know has a
horror story and they all go exactly

00:02:51.689 --> 00:02:55.949
like this: it was a week before the final
exam, they had just finished their

00:02:55.949 --> 00:02:59.310
outline for a class, it was so perfect
that the angels were singing.

00:02:59.310 --> 00:03:02.969
They were about to print it out and then
the computer went dead. They took their

00:03:02.969 --> 00:03:07.019
computer to every repair shop in the
state but nothing could be recovered.

00:03:07.019 --> 00:03:11.370
Everyone has a story like that, and
that's because you're going to thrash

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:15.780
your computer around in law school. Spend
the extra money and get what's called a

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:21.180
solid-state drive. It has no moving parts,
so it's much much more stable. Your

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:25.680
sanity is worth the premium for the
solid-state drive. Now on top of that, I

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:30.889
would strongly advise using Dropbox or
Google Drive some sort of cloud storage.

00:03:30.889 --> 00:03:35.159
Your outlines, your notes, your
assignments - they'll automatically be

00:03:35.159 --> 00:03:39.389
backed up, and it just looks exactly like
any kind of folder that you'll see on

00:03:39.389 --> 00:03:42.359
your computer anyway, so it's
indistinguishable from putting your

00:03:42.359 --> 00:03:46.259
files on your hard drive anyway. If
something happens to your laptop, all

00:03:46.259 --> 00:03:51.060
you'll have to do is log into your
account and download the latest version.

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:56.159
Finally, a laptop that has a big battery is
self explanatory. Some law school

00:03:56.159 --> 00:04:00.930
classrooms have plug-ins and some don't.
Sometimes you'll be in a study session

00:04:00.930 --> 00:04:04.979
for hours at a time - you never know when
you're going to have an electrical plug

00:04:04.979 --> 00:04:09.989
in and when you won't. So, these days it's
pretty standard for laptops to have

00:04:09.989 --> 00:04:15.479
eight, nine and ten hours of battery it's
worth it. It's so much better than having

00:04:15.479 --> 00:04:19.919
a laptop that needs to be plugged in
every hour or two. So for the most part I'm

00:04:19.919 --> 00:04:24.810
talking about Windows and
Macs. Why? Because you have to be able to

00:04:24.810 --> 00:04:30.450
run ExamSoft, and ExamSoft really only
runs on major laptops with normal

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:36.510
software on it. Your law school and your
Bar Examiners are almost all using ExamSoft,

00:04:36.510 --> 00:04:40.080
it's the software that locks out
your entire computer so the only thing

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:44.280
you can do is use a word processor for
purposes of your exam. It's the way

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:48.660
they make sure that no one can
cheat on the bar exam or on Law School

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:52.890
finals. So, it's important to have a
computer that can run that soft,

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:57.390
otherwise you will be totally screwed
when it comes to the final exam. So that

00:04:57.390 --> 00:05:01.560
brings me to the third thing that I wish
I had in law school and that is: a fast

00:05:01.560 --> 00:05:07.230
cheap laser printer. Now back in the day,
laser printers were the size of VW

00:05:07.230 --> 00:05:11.910
Beetles and they cost more than a new
kidney. Now they're the size of toasters

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:16.200
and cost about seven dollars. You can
pick up a reasonably fast laser printer

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:20.400
with a built-in scanner for less than
$200. In law school, you are going to be

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:25.410
printing a ton - whether it's your
outlines, your notes or flashcards you're

00:05:25.410 --> 00:05:29.400
going to be printing a lot and you want
a printer that can handle that. What's

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:32.669
great about a laser printer is that it's
unaffected by water, which is great

00:05:32.669 --> 00:05:36.090
because you're going to be drinking a
lot and you might happen to spill on

00:05:36.090 --> 00:05:39.810
your notes, which is the last thing you
want. If you can get a laser printer with a

00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:44.460
built-in scanner, even better. Those are
the three things that I wish I had when

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:50.010
I started law school. I use those three
things every day in practice - Technology

00:05:50.010 --> 00:05:54.540
has progressed so fast, there's so many
good tablets out there, so many good

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:58.620
laptops and so many good printers if you
make the investment upfront, if you don't

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:01.530
already have those things when you start
law school you'll be glad that you did.

00:06:01.530 --> 00:06:05.850
They're going to make your life so much
easier, and that's a huge part of

00:06:05.850 --> 00:06:10.140
succeeding in law school. Oh and one last
thing, if you're getting ready for law

00:06:10.140 --> 00:06:14.070
school check this out: we put together a
free e-book called the "Ultimate Pre-Law

00:06:14.070 --> 00:06:17.580
Checklist." Just click the link below to
download it. It's some of our best tips and

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:21.240
strategies for getting ahead before you
start law school, and it will put you

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:24.840
miles ahead of your classmates, just
click below. And also, if you like this

00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:28.350
video please subscribe to our channel we
come out with new videos on how to crush

00:06:28.350 --> 00:06:33.590
law school all the time. So thanks a lot
thanks for stopping by.

